From 440b3d147165d8ceaf8420d86bd9bb1dbce1689b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sunil Dora <sunilkumar.dora@windriver.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:40:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] meson: don't turn clang 23's -Wunused-but-set-global into an
 error

clang 23 added -Wunused-but-set-global to the -Wunused-but-set-variable
group, so the -Werror promotion in test_cflags now makes it fatal. It
fires on the parent_class variables that GLib's G_DEFINE_TYPE macros
emit whenever a type does not chain up:

  pango/pango-fontset.c:36:1: error: variable
  'pango_fontset_parent_class' set but not used
  [-Werror,-Wunused-but-set-global]

That code comes from the macro, not from pango. Keep the warning
visible but not fatal. gcc does not know this warning group, so
cc.get_supported_arguments() drops the flag there.

A GLib-side fix annotating the macro variable has been proposed
separately; this keeps pango building with released GLib either way.

Signed-off-by: Sunil Dora <sunilkumar.dora@windriver.com>
---
 meson.build | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 9a5dc9e..0fa5fc4 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -148,6 +148,10 @@ elif cc.get_id() == 'gcc' or cc.get_id() == 'clang'
     '-Werror=empty-body',
     '-Werror=write-strings',
     '-Werror=unused-but-set-variable',
+    # clang 23 added -Wunused-but-set-global to this group; it fires on the
+    # parent_class variables emitted by GLib's G_DEFINE_TYPE macros, which
+    # pango cannot fix here. Keep it a warning.
+    '-Wno-error=unused-but-set-global',
     '-Wundef', # FIXME: https://bugzilla.gnome.org/show_bug.cgi?id=792481
   ]
 
-- 
